                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is a healthy CAC for a D2C brand?</h3>
                                        <p>Depends on LTV. Aim for 3-5x LTV:CAC ratio. Below 3:1 is unsustainable long-term.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the difference between blended and paid CAC?</h3>
                                        <p>Blended = total marketing spend / total new customers. Paid CAC = paid-only. Blended is the truth; paid CAC understates real cost.</p>
                                        <h3>What is a normal payback period for D2C?</h3>
                                        <p>6-14 months. Above 24 months typically means the model is broken unless subscription-driven LTV is exceptional.</p>
                                        <h3>Why is my CAC rising?</h3>
                                        <p>Common causes: creative fatigue, narrow targeting, discount reliance, weak lifecycle, competitor auction pressure. Fix creative + lifecycle first.</p>
